From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 05:55:07 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: ov13858: Enable runtime PM before registering the
 subdev

On the Surface Pro 9 the rear camera sometimes comes up without its lens
actuator (no dw9800k VCM, no focus control) and the kernel logs

  ov13858 i2c-OVTID858:00: Error -13 runtime-resuming sensor, cannot instantiate VCM

Registering the subdev can complete the IPU bridge notifier at once when
the ISYS driver is already bound. Its bound callback schedules
ipu_bridge_instantiate_vcm_work(), which resumes the sensor with
pm_runtime_get_sync(). probe() enables runtime PM only after the
registration, so when the work runs first the resume fails with -EACCES
and the VCM client is never created. Whether probe() or the work wins
depends on timing: of two boots of the same kernel series one
instantiated the VCM and one did not.

Enable runtime PM before the subdev is registered and undo it when the
registration fails.

Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/ov13858.c | 18 ++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/ov13858.c b/drivers/media/i2c/ov13858.c
index 015493a16..e23e8362c 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov13858.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov13858.c
@@ -1856,21 +1856,27 @@ static int ov13858_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 		goto error_handler_free;
 	}
 
-	ret = v4l2_async_register_subdev_sensor(&ov13858->sd);
-	if (ret < 0)
-		goto error_media_entity;
-
 	/*
 	 * Device is already turned on by i2c-core with ACPI domain PM.
-	 * Enable runtime PM and turn off the device.
+	 * Enable runtime PM before the subdev is registered: registration can
+	 * complete the bridge's notifier, whose VCM instantiation work resumes
+	 * the sensor and fails with -EACCES while runtime PM is disabled.
 	 */
 	pm_runtime_set_active(ov13858->dev);
 	pm_runtime_enable(ov13858->dev);
+
+	ret = v4l2_async_register_subdev_sensor(&ov13858->sd);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		goto error_pm_disable;
+
+	/* Turn off the device. */
 	pm_runtime_idle(ov13858->dev);
 
 	return 0;
 
-error_media_entity:
+error_pm_disable:
+	pm_runtime_disable(ov13858->dev);
+	pm_runtime_set_suspended(ov13858->dev);
 	media_entity_cleanup(&ov13858->sd.entity);
 
 error_handler_free:
